# Last-handled neat-core version.
#
# Forests consumes neat-core via an unpinned `path` dependency that tracks head.
# CI (`scripts/check-neat-core-version.sh`) fails when the sibling neat-core
# presents a breaking bump above this baseline — pre-1.0 a higher minor, or any
# higher major — forcing a deliberate upgrade. Clear the gate by updating
# `forests` for the breaking change and bumping this version to match neat-core.
#
# 0.9.11 -> 0.10.0: acknowledge neat-core #569 (GRQ#4257), which retyped the
# public `MemeticExport::weights` field from
# `BTreeMap<String, Vec<MemeticWeightExport>>` to the new `MemeticWeights` enum
# so both valid wire forms parse. `forests` never names `MemeticExport` or any
# memetic weight type — its grafts only ever set `memetic: None` — so no code
# change is required. Verified by a clean `cargo build --release` and the full
# test suite passing against sibling neat-core 0.10.0.
# 0.10.0 -> 0.10.6: adopt neat-core #577, which keys synapse uniqueness by
# (fromUUID, toUUID, type) and lets an `IF` target read more than one role from
# the same source. That is what `--if-correction typed-pair` emits, and 0.10.5
# and earlier reject it. Nothing else changes: the default graft still uses the
# IDENTITY relay, which every version accepts. Verified by a clean
# `cargo build --release` and the full test suite against sibling neat-core
# 0.10.6.
# 0.10.6 -> 0.13.0: acknowledge neat-core #633 (Issue #625, 0.12.0), which made
# every `CompiledNetwork` field private behind borrow-only accessors so safe
# code can no longer edit a validated network into an out-of-bounds SIMD read,
# and 0.13.0 (#637, the security-scan milestone roll-up; nothing Forests names
# changed). Forests read `num_inputs` / `num_neurons` / `neurons` / `synapses`
# directly in `graft.rs` and `neurons` in `residuals.rs`; those reads now go
# through the `()` accessors. Unhandled, the same bump took the GRQ fleet down
# through rust_scorer (GRQ#4724); Forests was next in line because GRQ builds
# it from the same sibling neat-core at head. Verified by
# `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and the full test suite against
# the sibling clone at 0.13.0 (59eb6e6).
#
# 0.13.0 -> 0.17.0: acknowledge 0.14.0–0.17.0 so the breaking-bump gate can
# pass and scripts/runlib.sh can land (Issue #106). Forests does not name
# the 0.16.0 PruneResult fields or the 0.17.0 prune_neuron IF rewrite.
# Verified by `cargo check -p neat_ai_forests` against sibling 0.17.0.
#
# 0.17.0 -> 0.20.0 (Develop side, Issue #104): acknowledge 0.18.0-0.20.0 so
# the breaking-bump gate can pass and the canonical scripts/runlib.sh can
# land. The only library-visible break in that span is neat-core #682
# (0.19.0): `CreatureError` gains an `UnknownTargetUuid(String)` variant and
# `compile_creature` now refuses a synapse whose toUUID names no listed
# neuron. Forests never names `CreatureError` - `graft.rs` maps the error
# through `e.to_string()`, so the new variant needs no match arm - and its
# grafted `IF` subtrees only ever target neurons the creature lists. 0.18.0 is
# neat-core #684 (pruning corner cases across the JSON/WASM boundary) and
# 0.20.0 is neat-core #689 (the canonical runlib.sh itself); Forests names
# neither `PruneResult` nor `prune_neuron`. Verified by the full test suite -
# `cargo test --workspace --all-features`, including the real-scorer
# end-to-end graft and the TypeScript parity fixtures - passing against a
# sibling clone at 0.20.0.
#
# 0.17.0 -> 0.20.0 (PR #109 side): independently acknowledges the same
# 0.18.0-0.20.0 span against sibling neat-core at head. No forests code
# change is required:
#   * 0.18.0 (Ockham #196) is a documented-behaviour bump in
#     prune_neuron / prune_synapse — a target left with no inward edge takes
#     the bias fold. Forests never calls neat-core's prune API: its
#     `plan_prune` / `LearningsStore::prune` act on its own learnings JSONL.
#   * 0.19.0 (Issue #682) adds `CreatureError::UnknownTargetUuid` and makes
#     `compile_creature` refuse a synapse whose toUUID names no listed neuron.
#     Forests never matches exhaustively on `CreatureError` (it maps through
#     `.to_string()`), and its grafts always list every synapse target —
#     `creature_validate` runs before `compile_creature` on the graft path.
#   * 0.20.0 (Issue #680) canonicalises scripts/runlib.sh — a sibling-build
#     script change, not a neat-core public-API change. Forests' own
#     scripts/runlib.sh is tracked separately (Issue #104).
# Verified by `cargo check --workspace --all-targets`,
# `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, and
# the full `cargo test --workspace --all-features` suite against sibling 0.20.0.
0.20.0
